title incense clears its own gitignored build cache, buying pier headroom
prompt Continue the incense captain's overnight/day lap: open the baton and inner prompt, find the next agent-doable item, and work it honestly.
think The card's live INCENSE row named a real, unresolved fault: the shared root filesystem at 96 to 97 percent full, 5.5 to 7.6G free, and a cold endurance run dying with no run_verdict= line -- the same silent death REDS %745 named for the /tmp pen leak, one layer over.
think The row asked two open questions: the pier's own disk headroom, and which ship's gitignored build-cache rooms are safe to clear. Measured per ship with git status --porcelain --ignored=matching plus du -s: 3.7G to 14.8G gitignored bytes per checkout, roughly 82G fleet-wide, almost entirely compiled */bin/ witness and CLI binaries under named .gitignore lines -- rebuildable output, never tracked.
think Captaincy reaches a shared-resource fault (the mount itself) without touching a peer's authored tree, the same boundary REDS %745 drew for the /tmp reclaim. So I cleared only incense's own */bin/ rooms -- 24 directories, each confirmed git check-ignore before removal -- and left rye/bin and rishi/bin (the load-bearing toolchain binaries) untouched.
think Verified the clear was safe rather than assumed: git status --porcelain read clean afterward (nothing tracked touched), and tools/ca/caravan_reclaim_witness.rish rebuilt from the cleared cache and read GREEN, proving the cost is rebuild time alone.
think REDS.md stood at 10 bytes of headroom, pin_deadlocked=1, per the card's own prior note -- could not add a row without folding one first. %795 was the one fully CLOSED row on the pin (no OPEN tail), 3,641 bytes, built and proven on its own lap; folded it to a shelf per the-writer-sheds and stamp-and-name, freeing room for the new row.
think Booked the new row by stamp rather than by a %N the derive tool would have handed me wrong: sh tools/fixtures/r/reds_spine_derive_scan.sh --next answered 828, but %828 already exists (born CLOSED, folded straight to a shelf, never landing as a live REDS.md body row) -- a real gap in that tool's own reading, not mine to fix mid-lap. Grepped every %NNN header across REDS.md and every archive shelf to find the true max (828) and followed the two most recent rows' own precedent of citing by stamp alone rather than guessing a number.
think Shed my own account on ITINERARY.md too: the live disk-headroom paragraph became a shelved-account pointer, same as every other INCENSE row on the card, keeping the pin under its own bound.
think Proved the touched pins clean: ascii_document_scan.sh reads chars=748 against ceiling=750, verdict=ok; tracked_link_scan.sh read living_links_outside_tree=3 before staging (the new files were untracked) and 0 after git add, verdict=ok; reds_ledger_monotone_witness.rish and itinerary_list_witness.rish both GREEN.
obs The single highest-leverage safe action on a shared, near-full pier is clearing one's own rebuildable, gitignored build output -- it costs nothing but rebuild time, and on a shared mount the freed headroom serves every ship immediately, without touching a byte of any peer's tree.
obs The other seven ships' own build-cache rooms (roughly 68G of the fleet-wide 82G) stay theirs to clear on their own touch, per one-writer-per-checkout; named on the shelved account rather than swept.
rota lap 6586, row 1 -- Air, feels. What the tree felt like today: a pier holding its own weight against a nearly-full disk, and a deadlocked ledger pin with ten bytes of headroom -- both cleared by the same motion, freeing room to breathe before naming the next word.
loom caravan_reclaim_witness=green rebuild_from_cleared_cache=yes df_before=96pct_7.6G_free df_after=89pct_20G_free cleared_bytes_incense=approx_12.5G
file glow/bin caravan/bin mycelium/bin image/bin crypto/bin pond/bin brushstroke/bin lotus/bin constel/bin mantra/bin linengrow/bin -- 24 gitignored build-output directories removed after git check-ignore confirmation, rebuildable, incense's own tree only
file construction/REDS.md -- %795 folded to a shelf to clear the deadlocked pin; new row booked by stamp 20260925.130901, disk-headroom repair recorded with three fields
file construction/archive/REDS/REDS-a-lantern-that-fired-twice-rows-795.md -- the shelved %795 row, CLOSED, immutable
file construction/archive/REDS/REDS-fold-recital.md -- one line recording the %795 fold
file construction/ITINERARY.md -- the live disk-headroom paragraph replaced with a shelved-account pointer, keeping the pin under its 40960-byte bound
file construction/archive/date/20260925/20260925-130901_itinerary-incense-disk-headroom-account.md -- the shelved account, full per-ship gitignored-byte table and what stays open
recommend kg -- the pier has real headroom again (20G free); next lap can safely launch the cold endurance run per the baton's ORDER clause and take the next agent-doable item.
